   "source": [
    "# 3. Data Preparation\n",
    "\n",
    "Data preparation converts the raw dataset into a modelling-ready structure. This includes filtering to working-age individuals, checking duplicates, correcting data types, creating a binary target variable and removing features that would create data leakage.\n",
    "\n",
    "This stage is critical because a model can appear highly accurate for the wrong reason if it is trained with variables that directly reveal the target outcome — a problem known as data leakage (Géron, 2022)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "7fc9ac28-4018-4814-a2ef-acb9a06325cb",
