   "source": [
    "### Data Understanding Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The exploratory analysis shows that the dataset contains meaningful variation across age, education, employment status and demographic groups. It also shows that some demographic categories are much larger than others. This matters for fairness auditing because subgroup metrics are generally more reliable when groups have sufficient sample sizes (Bellamy et al., 2019).\n",
    "\n",
    "The descriptive analysis should therefore be used as context for the modelling results. If a group is small or structurally different from another group, differences in model performance should be interpreted carefully rather than treated as immediate proof of discrimination."
   ]
