   "source": [
    "## Feature Selection Discussion\n",
    "\n",
    "The final feature set is deliberately restricted to variables that are defensible for an audit-oriented proof-of-concept. The selected variables are used to simulate the type of structured applicant or population profile that an organisation might audit for disparities.\n",
    "\n",
    "The retained variables include:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `AGEP`: age;\n",
    "- `SEX`: sex category;\n",
    "- `SCHL`: educational attainment;\n",
    "- `RAC1P`: race-related category;\n",
    "- `HISP`: Hispanic origin;\n",
    "- `DIS`: disability status.\n",
    "\n",
    "The removed variables are not removed because they are statistically unimportant. They are removed because they would create leakage or would be too closely connected to the employment outcome. This supports a fairer and more realistic audit design."
   ]
  },
  {
